# s2u-yt — managed yt-dlp config (installed into ~/.local/share/s2u-yt/conf/config).
#
# This file is applied AFTER your ~/.config/yt-dlp/config via --config-locations,
# so anything you already have (cookies, js runtimes, ...) keeps working and this
# file wins on any conflict.
#
# Client strategy — NO pinned player_client (2026-08-22):
#
# YouTube's SABR/range enforcement (2026-08) broke the previous pin
# (`android_vr,web_safari`): android_vr URLs came back answering **403 to
# plain GETs and open-ended `Range: bytes=0-`** — exactly what mpv/ffmpeg
# and MPD send — while `yt-dlp -J` still exited 0, so the wrapper's
# authenticated fallback never fired. Verified live 2026-08-22 with
# yt-dlp 2026.08.19: with NO client pin, the default client order reaches
# the new anonymous **VISIONOS** client, whose URLs answer **200 to plain
# GETs** (and 206 to open ranges, after a 302 redirect) — mpv, ffprobe
# and MPD all play them.
#
# Do NOT re-pin `player_client` here without re-verifying end-to-end:
# every pinned combination tested (web/mweb/web_safari variants) steered
# selection onto range-restricted audio formats (403s), and an
# authenticated session alone lands on WEB_EMBEDDED_PLAYER (fully 403).
#
# PO tokens: still minted by the bgutil provider (systemd --user unit
# s2u-yt-bgutil.service); keep it running (status.sh checks it). If the
# anonymous pass ever fails, the wrapper's phase-2 authenticated retry
# (user cookies) still applies.
